 {"candidate_version":"source-preserving-format-display-v3-complete-action-syntax","source_id":"SRC_83ce9780d89a2977b94257ad","original_answer_sha256":"57cfe0f6a8cab6021b272591711f957ede45b41f82435919c1a8c1a5044fcc69","view_sha256":"57cfe0f6a8cab6021b272591711f957ede45b41f82435919c1a8c1a5044fcc69","offset_convention":"Python Unicode code points; end exclusive; no normalization","rows":[{"text":"**Chosen Method:** FDISCO","original_unit_ids":["L0001"],"original_character_ranges":[[0,25]]},{"text":"**Chosen Labeling:** [GFP (内源)+Alexa Fluor 488, MAP2+Alexa Fluor 594, DAPI]","original_unit_ids":["L0002"],"original_character_ranges":[[26,101]]},{"text":"**Justification:** FDISCO is specifically optimized for preserving weak endogenous fluorescence (like GFP/YFP) by maintaining an alkaline environment (pH 9.0) throughout the dehydration and clearing process, which prevents the quenching of fluorescent proteins common in other solvent-based methods. For a 3 mm thick brain block, FDISCO provides superior transparency and refractive index matching (RI ≈ 1.56) compared to aqueous methods, ensuring high-resolution 3D imaging of fine dendritic branches. The dual-labeling strategy uses Alexa Fluor 488 to boost the weak endogenous GFP signal and MAP2 to provide a detailed dendritic scaffold, while the pH-adjusted DBE allows for stable long-term storage (up to 6 months) at 4 ℃.","original_unit_ids":["L0003"],"original_character_ranges":[[102,830]]},{"text":"**Protocol Steps:**","original_unit_ids":["L0004"],"original_character_ranges":[[831,850]]},{"text":"1 Pre-clearing Immunostaining (Pre-treatment)","original_unit_ids":["L0005"],"original_character_ranges":[[851,896]]},{"text":"Incubation with PTx2 solution (PBS with 0.2% Triton X-100) for permeabilization. (Temperature: RT, Time: 6 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0006"],"original_character_ranges":[[897,1010]]},{"text":"Incubation with Blocking Solution (PTx2, 10% Normal Goat Serum, and 5% DMSO). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 12 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0007"],"original_character_ranges":[[1011,1124]]},{"text":"Incubation with Primary Antibodies (Anti-GFP and Anti-MAP2, 1:500 dilution in PTwH: PBS with 0.2% Tween-20 and 10 μg/ml Heparin). (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 72 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0008"],"original_character_ranges":[[1125,1290]]},{"text":"Incubation with PTwH solution for washing (5 changes). (Temperature: RT, Time: 10 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0009"],"original_character_ranges":[[1291,1379]]},{"text":"Incubation with Secondary Antibodies (Alexa Fluor 488 and Alexa Fluor 594, 1:500) and DAPI (1:1000) in PTwH. (Temperature: 37 ℃, Time: 72 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0010"],"original_character_ranges":[[1380,1524]]},{"text":"Incubation with PTwH solution for final washing (5 changes). (Temperature: RT, Time: 10 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0011"],"original_character_ranges":[[1525,1619]]},{"text":"2 Dehydration (FDISCO)","original_unit_ids":["L0012"],"original_character_ranges":[[1620,1642]]},{"text":"Incubation with 50% (vol/vol) Tetrahydrofuran (THF) in distilled water, pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0013"],"original_character_ranges":[[1643,1787]]},{"text":"Incubation with 70% (vol/vol) THF in distilled water, pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0014"],"original_character_ranges":[[1788,1914]]},{"text":"Incubation with 80% (vol/vol) THF in distilled water, pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0015"],"original_character_ranges":[[1915,2041]]},{"text":"Incubation with 100% (vol/vol) THF (peroxide-free), pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0016"],"original_character_ranges":[[2042,2166]]},{"text":"Incubation with a second round of 100% (vol/vol) THF, pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 2 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0017"],"original_character_ranges":[[2167,2293]]},{"text":"Clearing and RI Matching","original_unit_ids":["L0018"],"original_character_ranges":[[2294,2318]]},{"text":"Incubation with Dibenzyl ether (DBE), pH adjusted to 9.0 with Triethylamine, until the tissue becomes completely transparent. (Temperature: RT, Time: 4 hours)","original_unit_ids":["L0019"],"original_character_ranges":[[2319,2477]]},{"text":"4 Preservation and Imaging","original_unit_ids":["L0020"],"original_character_ranges":[[2478,2504]]},{"text":"4.1 Storage in fresh pH-adjusted DBE in a glass vial, protected from light and sealed to prevent oxidation. (Temperature: 4 ℃, Time: 6 months)","original_unit_ids":["L0021"],"original_character_ranges":[[2505,2647]]},{"text":"4.2 Pre-imaging mounting in a custom chamber filled with pH-adjusted DBE (RI = 1.56). (Temperature: RT, Time: 1 hour)","original_unit_ids":["L0022"],"original_character_ranges":[[2648,2765]]}],"removed_structural_prefixes":[],"nonformat_content_and_order_exact":true}
 
